      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The labor in Eastern Europe is generally more reliable and accustomed to Western standards, requiring less hand-holding. Southeast Asia offers a large, adaptable workforce, though quality control can vary depending on the specific factory management. Sub-Saharan Africa presents the most significant challenges, often requiring intensive, on-the-ground management to ensure consistent output and adherence to strict KPIs.",
